senses.gloss:
puraṃdhi,
 —1. a. courageous, highspirited,
 exalted;
 —2. as m. perhaps as
name of a god, Purandhi;
 —3. as f. exaltation.

purástāt, adv.
 —1. before; in the front,
85^18;
 —2. previously, afore, 98^6, 10111, 13;
 —3. before, i. e. (see prāñc) eastward;
 —4. prep. w. gen. [1130], before, in the
presence of, 20^1. [puras, 1100b.]

puraḥ-sará, a. going before; as m. forerunner;
 at end of cpds [1302c 2], having
…as forerunner, i. e. accompanied by…;
…-puraḥsaram, adv. with…or after….

pū́rva [525^4], a. being before in place or
time:
 —1. east (cf. prāñc);
 —2. prior;
preceding, 86^13; pūrva…uttara, former
…latter, 21^8; ancient, 57^6; of old time,
69^3, 83^10; first spoken, 60^2; w. past pass.
ppl. [1291]: dṛṣṭa-pūrva, seen before;
pūrvam, adv. before; beforehand, 60^9;
previously, already, 7^21, 25^17; in former
times, 48^1; long ago, 46^3; first, 103^6;
pūrvam…uttaram, first…last, 104^12;
 —3. at end of cpds, (having…as preceding
thing, i. e.) accompanied by…, or
simply with…, 8^21. [connected w. puras
and pra.]
